    "craft": {
      "type": "section",
      "blocks": {
        "jumbo": {
          "type": "jumbo-text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "Six metres.\nOne weaver.\nMany weeks.",
            "font": "heading",
            "alignment": "left",
            "line_height": "1",
            "letter_spacing": "-0.03em",
            "case": "none",
            "text_effect": "reveal",
            "animation_repeat": false,
            "text_color": "#fdfbf7"
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "body": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>A silk saree is woven on a handloom, thread by thread. The zari border is worked separately and joined to the body by hand, and the pallu alone can take a weaver several days. Nothing about it is quick, which is rather the point.</p>",
            "width": "100%",
            "max_width": "normal",
            "alignment": "left",
            "type_preset": "rte",
            "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
